# Tasks: LOOP-PROTECTION

Purpose:
  Define the loop protection system that prevents the AI autonomous
  execution loop from spinning infinitely. Five automated guards plus
  one human escalation guard ensure that the AI never repeats the
  same failing approach without adding value.

Owns:

  Loop guards (5 automated + 1 human)
  LOOP_SCORE calculation
  Loop risk thresholds
  Strategy change rules
  Retry vs Repeat enforcement

TrustHierarchy:
  1. Explicit project constraints (project-level policy)
  2. Decisions (bax decisions/)
  3. Validated project skills (bax skills/)
  4. Established organization knowledge (bax references/)
  5. General best practices (bax references/best-practices/)
  6. AI suggestions (lowest priority)

Guards:

  1. MaxIterations
     definition: total iteration count for a task
     config: max_iterations (per EXECUTION-CONTRACT.sdd)
     action on breach: ESCALATE with reason

  2. FailureBudget
     definition: weighted failure allowance (severity-weighted)
     config: max_failure_budget (per EXECUTION-CONTRACT.sdd)
     weighting: minor=1, major=2, critical=5
     action on breach: ESCALATE with reason

  3. NoProgressDetection
     definition: consecutive iterations with no meaningful change
     detection: same failure count across N iterations
     action on trigger: LOOP_RISK_HIGH, strategy change required

  4. DuplicateActionDetection
     definition: same action + same reasoning applied repeatedly
     detection: action signature + reasoning hash compared across attempts
     action on trigger: DUPLICATE_ATTEMPT, block same approach

  5. StateTransitionRules
     definition: allowed state transitions are constrained
     rule: TESTING -> FIXING -> TESTING is permitted only with
           progress evidence (bax TASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd -> ProgressRule)
     rule: ESCALATED and COMPLETED are terminal
     rule: BLOCKED cannot be bypassed without blocker resolution

  6. HumanEscalation
     definition: 6th guard — human review triggers
     triggers:
       - irreversible decision
       - security concern
       - ambiguous requirement
       - conflicting architecture
       - missing external dependency
       - budget exceeded
       - high-risk migration
     action: pause autonomous execution, request human input

LOOP_SCORE:

  Calculation:
    same_action:      +30   (same approach attempted again)
    same_error:       +25   (same error encountered again)
    no_progress:      +30   (consecutive iterations without measurable change)
    plan_reverted:    +20   (plan changed back to previous version)
    new_evidence:     -20   (genuinely new information discovered)
    meaningful_change: -30  (measurable improvement: fewer failures, fewer errors)

  Scoring example:
    iteration 3: tried repository fix (same_action +30)
                 same deadlock error (same_error +25)
                 3 failures before, 3 failures now (no_progress +30)
                 loop_score = 85

  Threshold:
    LOOP_SCORE >= 60  -> LOOP_RISK_HIGH
    action: require new strategy, do NOT retry same approach

  Enforcement:
    LOOP_RISK_HIGH -> AI MUST switch strategy
    LOOP_RISK_HIGH + loop_score >= 90 -> ESCALATE to human

StrategyChange:

  Rules:
    [SP1] When LOOP_RISK_HIGH, AI MUST adopt Strategy B (different approach).
    [SP2] Strategy A can only be revisited if NEW evidence emerges that
          was not present when Strategy A was abandoned.
    [SP3] Each strategy MUST be attempted at most once per evidence set.
    [SP4] Strategy change MUST be recorded with reason and evidence delta.

  Example:
    Strategy A: repository fix         (failed: deadlock persists)
    Strategy B: application service redesign  (attempt)
    Strategy C: architecture / context investigation  (if B fails)
    Return to A: only if new evidence about locking model discovered

RetryVsRepeat:

  ALLOW:
    retry when new evidence AND new strategy are present
  BLOCK:
    same evidence + same strategy + same result = repeat (forbidden)

  Distinction:
    Retry:  Eyni məqsədə yeni məlumatla yenidən cəhd.
    Repeat: Eyni şeyi heç nə dəyişmədən yenidən etmək.

Rules:

  [LP1] The 5 automated guards ALWAYS run concurrently during execution.
  [LP2] LOOP_SCORE is recalculated after every iteration within a
        TESTING -> FIXING -> TESTING cycle.
  [LP3] LOOP_SCORE >= 60 requires a strategy change — AI MUST NOT
        retry the same approach.
  [LP4] Human escalation is the final guard — it can trigger at any
        LOOP_SCORE if the escalation conditions in section 6 are met.
  [LP5] AI MUST NOT continue in TESTING -> FIXING -> TESTING cycle
        when no meaningful progress is detected across iterations.
  [LP6] Failure budget is severity-weighted, not a simple failure count.
  [LP7] Strategy A may only be revisited with genuinely new evidence.
  [LP8] Retry (new evidence + new strategy) is required; Repeat is
        blocked.
  [LP9] All loop guard triggers MUST be recorded in the execution trace.
  [LP10] When all strategies are exhausted within the iteration budget,
         the task MUST be ESCALATED.

